ASSUMPTION CHALLENGE
Vertices considered: runners, 3-term relations, fold gates, additive-energy fibres, exact witnesses, proof buckets.
Chosen quotient: proof buckets plus relation diagnostics.
Preserved predicate: whether exact M(S) clears delta and which proof route plausibly explains the clearance.
Destroyed information: exact endpoint-cover components and prime-fibre certificates; those re-enter via HYP-2112/Phi and the paper sieve.
Challenged assumption: 4-term additive structure is a hard signal by itself; in this sample it is noise unless it carries a 3-term fold.
